<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roossenekal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roossenekal is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpumalanga">Mpumalanga</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middelburg">Middelburg</a>. It was founded after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mabhoko">Mapoch</a> War of 1882–1883 near the former Ndzundza <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndebele-kingdom">Ndebele</a> stronghold of KwaMaza and named after Roos and Senekal, two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> officers killed in that war. Nearby are the caves where the Ndebele held out against the South African Republic's siege.</p></div>
